{"agent":"lane1-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"A git or cwd failure while identifying the caller is treated as “foreign”, so a legitimate import from the caller’s own linked worktree is refused. `W.current(Path(os.getcwd()))` is wrapped in `except Exception: own = None`, and the only allow-path is `own is not None and own.path.resolve() == foreign.worktree.resolve()`. Given the editable install pointing at the caller’s worktree (the case the comment calls legitimate) and `os.getcwd()` raising `FileNotFoundError` because the cwd was removed, or `W.current` raising because git cannot be read, `own` stays None, `repoint_shared_editable` runs, and the function returns `FAIL`. That contradicts the same function’s contract that a git or env failure must not block every command (the `foreign_launch_root` failure path returns `OK`).","digest":"59670f954e6b6392","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/surfaces/cli.py:_guard_foreign_launch","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/cli.py:_guard_foreign_launch"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The heal that is supposed to stop the next process importing the doomed tree does not update the file that actually controls imports unless the `.pth` text is exactly `str(foreign.resolve())`. `direct_url.json` is matched after `Path(...).resolve()`, but the `.pth` check is `read_text().strip() == str(foreign_resolved)`, and a miss is swallowed. Given a shared editable `.pth` whose line is the path pip recorded, `[REDACTED:path]`, while that path’s `resolve()` is `/private/home/dev/proj/.ddflow/worktrees/lane-a` (symlink prefix, typical on macOS), the URL may be rewritten and `changed` may become True, but the `.pth` is left pointing at `lane-a`. The CLI still prints that the install “was reset” and returns `FAIL`. The re-run adds the same `.pth` line to `sys.path`, imports that lane again, and refuses again, so the ModuleNotFoundError crash is replaced by a permanent lockout until the `.pth` is fixed by hand.","digest":"f072f724b5c17c36","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/install_info.py:repoint_shared_editable","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/install_info.py:repoint_shared_editable"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The suite locks in the wrong predicate for B-cli-ran-code-from-another-lanes-worktree. The bug and this file's own docstring say the caller's own linked worktree is a legitimate import root and only another lane's tree is not, but `test_running_from_a_linked_worktree_is_detected_as_foreign` sets `PATHS.package_parent` to the process's own worktree and asserts `foreign_launch_root()` is that tree. `repoint_shared_editable` is only exercised as \"anything not the primary must be rewritten to the primary\". Given a lane whose cwd and imported tree are both its own worktree (no other lane), this passes only if the CLI treats that launch as foreign and rewrites the shared editable install away from the caller's tree — the failure mode the bug said must remain allowed, and the same shared-venv rewrite the report guessed caused the crash.","digest":"ab6b87d32a6e7b74","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_foreign_worktree_import.py:44","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_foreign_worktree_import.py:44"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12016,"diff_sha":"1bc712ce8b85c84d5e44e7ba20293d412ff69bb5e852e0aceda4c3582d23be7f","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-cli-ran-code-from-another-lanes-worktree","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":149.9,"family":"xai","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"d67a2ef19b9cd727","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-cli-ran-code-from-another-lanes-worktree.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261110T224055Z-494c9b99.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"94e998d7520c3e8bf5876f967d014168810249e1","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/install_info.py":"100644 9be3b3424febe4d567032840b1fae65de2dcbf0f","ddflow/surfaces/cli.py":"100644 a5a6044df49e73bdc42261ed22fc1c281e101027","tests/test_foreign_worktree_import.py":"100644 86abbaf444b8b2b4af42d1ec4bf77eb0c422823f"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/cli.py:_guard_foreign_launch","ddflow/services/install_info.py:repoint_shared_editable","tests/test_foreign_worktree_import.py:44"],"tree_sha":"94e998d7520c+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"eb6f94210832a3a663c0c09c5","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":168215,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-cli-ran-code-from-another-lanes-worktree","ts":"2026-11-10T22:43:25.523368Z"}
