{"agent":"lane1-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"A git or cwd lookup failure is treated as “not the caller’s tree” and still rewrites the shared install. If this process was imported from the caller’s own linked worktree (legitimate) and `W.current(Path(os.getcwd()))` raises, `own` is set to None, the `own.path.resolve() == foreign.worktree.resolve()` check is skipped, and `repoint_shared_editable` runs before `return FAIL`. That retargets the shared editable install away from the caller’s tree and blocks the command, which contradicts the function’s own rule that a git/env failure must not keep commands from running.","digest":"0afea2b01702e2ea","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/surfaces/cli.py:_guard_foreign_launch","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/cli.py:_guard_foreign_launch"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The file that actually puts the foreign tree on `sys.path` is often left unchanged, while the CLI always claims the install was reset. The `.pth` is updated only when its text equals `str(foreign.resolve())`. The string Python imported from (and that pip wrote) is `str(foreign)` before symlink resolution — e.g. `.pth` contains `/tmp/lane` while `resolve()` is `/private/tmp/lane` — so the write is skipped. `direct_url.json` is matched via `Path.resolve()`, so metadata can move to the primary while the `.pth` still names the doomed worktree. `_guard_foreign_launch` ignores the `False` return and prints that the install was reset; the re-run imports the same foreign tree and is refused again.","digest":"1dd4f6b13680c311","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/install_info.py:repoint_shared_editable","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/install_info.py:repoint_shared_editable"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The regression locks in the wrong notion of \"foreign\". The bug text says a launch is bad only when the imported tree is another lane's worktree, and that the caller's own tree is legitimate. `checkout` sets `PATHS.package_parent` to the linked worktree the process is running from, and `test_running_from_a_linked_worktree_is_detected_as_foreign` then requires `foreign_launch_root()` to return that same tree. Given a normal lane launch whose code comes from `.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-hy-stop-protocol` (the caller), this test demands a foreign hit, so a fix that satisfies it will repoint or abort that run. The case that actually crashed — import root is lane B while the caller is lane A or primary — is never constructed, so the stated failure can still pass these tests.","digest":"1c720847a94a6a05","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_foreign_worktree_import.py:44","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"tests/test_foreign_worktree_import.py:44"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12016,"diff_sha":"1bc712ce8b85c84d5e44e7ba20293d412ff69bb5e852e0aceda4c3582d23be7f","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-cli-ran-code-from-another-lanes-worktree","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":88.4,"family":"xai","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"1eaadec962df97ff","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-cli-ran-code-from-another-lanes-worktree.critic.grok-4.7.20261110T224331Z-adb79c04.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"94e998d7520c3e8bf5876f967d014168810249e1","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/install_info.py":"100644 9be3b3424febe4d567032840b1fae65de2dcbf0f","ddflow/surfaces/cli.py":"100644 a5a6044df49e73bdc42261ed22fc1c281e101027","tests/test_foreign_worktree_import.py":"100644 86abbaf444b8b2b4af42d1ec4bf77eb0c422823f"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/cli.py:_guard_foreign_launch","ddflow/services/install_info.py:repoint_shared_editable","tests/test_foreign_worktree_import.py:44"],"tree_sha":"94e998d7520c+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"e1ac2f59e360901287b390f99","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":168230,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-cli-ran-code-from-another-lanes-worktree","ts":"2026-11-10T22:45:00.166119Z"}
